WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.196 --> 00:00:16.962
The children followed Julio out of the church and into the street.

2
00:00:18.143 --> 00:00:21.684
The streets of Palos were busy with people carrying goods.

3
00:00:22.824 --> 00:00:27.406
They were carrying supplies in their hands, in wagons, and on animals.

4
00:00:28.707 --> 00:00:32.680
Everyone was heading in the same direction: to the docks.

5
00:00:33.861 --> 00:00:36.801
Julio led the children in that direction as well.

6
00:00:38.042 --> 00:00:40.863
Mandy could smell the ocean before she saw it.

7
00:00:40.883 --> 00:00:44.084
"Mandy, look!"

8
00:00:44.584 --> 00:00:45.364
cried Vinnie.

9
00:00:46.544 --> 00:00:48.625
At the end of the street was the harbor.

10
00:00:49.805 --> 00:00:52.706
Vinnie pointed to three ships tied up at the pier.

11
00:00:54.046 --> 00:00:55.887
One was bigger than the other two.

12
00:00:55.907 --> 00:00:59.528
"The biggest one is—," began Julio.

13
00:01:00.668 --> 00:01:01.909
"The Santa Maria.

14
00:01:03.189 --> 00:01:06.851
And the others are the Pinta and Niña," said Vinnie.

15
00:01:07.951 --> 00:01:09.312
Julio looked impressed.

16
00:01:09.332 --> 00:01:14.414
"You'd better return that book to Columbus," Julio said to Mandy.

17
00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:16.735
"He won't sail without it."

18
00:01:16.755 --> 00:01:19.396
"Where can I find him?"

19
00:01:20.016 --> 00:01:20.716
asked Mandy.

20
00:01:20.736 --> 00:01:25.738
"Aboard the Santa Maria, of course," replied Julio.

21
00:01:25.758 --> 00:01:28.119
"Can you take us there?"

22
00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:29.520
said Mandy.

23
00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:34.721
"Sure, come on," Julio said, waving his hand.

24
00:01:36.082 --> 00:01:38.182
They walked down the street to the pier.

25
00:01:39.623 --> 00:01:40.923
The harbor was busy.

26
00:01:42.223 --> 00:01:45.604
Men were loading all kinds of equipment onto the ships.

27
00:01:46.845 --> 00:01:48.805
Seagulls circled above the waves.

28
00:01:50.126 --> 00:01:53.186
Along the way, they asked Julio more questions.

29
00:01:53.206 --> 00:01:57.228
"Why are the sailors afraid of sailing west?"

30
00:01:57.848 --> 00:01:58.588
Mandy asked.

31
00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.041
Julio took a breath.

32
00:02:03.282 --> 00:02:05.382
He was still nervous about the trip.

33
00:02:05.402 --> 00:02:09.524
"It is said that sea monsters live in those waters.

34
00:02:10.845 --> 00:02:15.787
Even if you somehow sail past them, well Julio paused.

35
00:02:16.987 --> 00:02:18.708
"The ocean ends at some point.

36
00:02:19.929 --> 00:02:20.889
Then what happens?"

37
00:02:20.909 --> 00:02:24.991
"Oh, don't worry.

38
00:02:25.951 --> 00:02:27.092
The world is round.

39
00:02:28.692 --> 00:02:31.414
Your ship won't fall," laughed Vinnie.

40
00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:34.195
"How do you know what is out there?"

41
00:02:34.816 --> 00:02:36.317
Julio said angrily.

42
00:02:36.337 --> 00:02:40.119
"I bet you haven't been on an adventure in your life!"

43
00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.142
Vinnie and Mandy smiled at each other and thought of their photo trips.

44
00:02:46.162 --> 00:02:49.324
"Julio!" someone called.

45
00:02:50.665 --> 00:02:53.006
A middle-aged woman approached them.

46
00:02:54.287 --> 00:02:56.168
She was carrying a wool blanket.

47
00:02:57.332 --> 00:02:58.633
"Señora Molina!

48
00:02:58.953 --> 00:03:00.514
What a pleasant surprise!"

49
00:03:01.335 --> 00:03:02.896
Julio cried happily.

50
00:03:03.997 --> 00:03:06.178
He introduced the children to her.

51
00:03:06.198 --> 00:03:09.440
"Señora Molina owns a wool shop.

52
00:03:10.541 --> 00:03:14.063
Her wool is the softest and warmest in all of Spain."

53
00:03:14.083 --> 00:03:20.348
"Here, take this," said Señora Molina, handing the blanket to Julio.

54
00:03:20.368 --> 00:03:23.730
"This will keep you warm on cold nights."

55
00:03:24.931 --> 00:03:27.733
"Thank you so much," Julio said.

56
00:03:29.054 --> 00:03:29.774
He hugged her.

57
00:03:29.794 --> 00:03:35.098
"Be careful, Julio," she whispered, wiping her eyes.

58
00:03:36.379 --> 00:03:41.942
Julio waved good-bye, then he and Mandy and Vinnie continued onto the pier.

59
00:03:41.963 --> 00:03:49.948
"One day I will make Spanish wool famous," said Julio, holding the soft blanket close to him.

60
00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:52.790
"How?" asked Vinnie.

61
00:03:52.810 --> 00:04:00.299
"When I have my own ship, I will sell wool at every port on earth," Julio said proudly.

62
00:04:00.319 --> 00:04:06.402
"Maybe you'll become an explorer like Columbus," said Mandy.

63
00:04:06.422 --> 00:04:08.984
"Who wants to be like him?"

64
00:04:09.484 --> 00:04:10.485
replied Julio.

65
00:04:10.505 --> 00:04:14.187
"He's a dreamer with some crazy ideas."

66
00:04:14.207 --> 00:04:16.688
"But look at him now!"

67
00:04:17.349 --> 00:04:18.449
exclaimed Mandy.

68
00:04:18.469 --> 00:04:21.111
"Look at what?"

69
00:04:21.591 --> 00:04:22.552
Julio laughed.

70
00:04:23.521 --> 00:04:25.590
"He hasn't discovered anything yet!"
